import { PracticalCollectionCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> PracticalCollectionCopy = PracticalCollectionCopy {
  summary: "items.filter keeps every List element whose condition function returns True. The returned List preserves their original order and leaves the input contents unchanged.",
  taskTitle: "List all urgent tasks",
  purpose: "From Read, Review, and Ship, select every task whose urgent field is True. Display both Review and Ship, then check the original list and an empty input.",
  typescriptBefore: "For a normal array, filter keeps urgent tasks and map extracts their titles for display. This is idiomatic TypeScript and leaves the original array unchanged. The final call applies the same predicate to the typed empty array none. The array compares the task without reproducing List’s representation.",
  benefit: "Seseragi also accepts one function to decide which records to keep. The condition has type Task -> Bool and the result is List<Task>. As in TypeScript, the selection can be made while keeping the original collection available.",
  setup: "struct Task defines a record type with title: String and urgent: Bool; Task { ... } constructs a value. The backtick before tasks’ opening bracket creates a List. Brackets without a backtick create an Array. items is the alias for std/list.",
  after: [
    "fn urgent task: Task -> Bool = task.urgent takes one task and returns its urgent Bool field. items.filter urgent tasks passes the condition function first and the List second. urgent is passed as a function to apply to elements, rather than called once at that point.",
    "selected is List<Task>. The comprehension [task.title | task <- selected] takes each task from selected and creates an Array of titles. These brackets have no leading backtick. Its JSON display is [\"Review\",\"Ship\"].",
    "The next line displays titles from the original tasks, so Read, Review, and Ship are all still there. The final items.empty<Task> () creates an empty List<Task>. Filtering it also gives an empty result, displayed as [].",
  ],
  details: [
    "filter applies the condition to every element from the beginning and keeps the True matches in their original order. Multiple matches are all retained; no matches produce an empty List. An empty input does not call the condition function.",
    "The condition must accept Task and return Bool. Returning its title String does not mean “keep it if it has text.” Here task.urgent already has type Bool, so it can be returned directly.",
    "Elements with values 0, False, or an empty string are retained when the condition returns True. filter does not automatically coerce each element to a truth value and discard it. A condition that selects False values can produce a List containing False.",
    "Use find when only the first match is needed. filter returns all matching elements as List; find returns the first as Maybe. Choose based on the result the task needs.",
  ],
}
